 | `art/baked/boot/village.glb` | The village kit: the parts the street's houses are put together from (a stone foot with its drip board, upright and lying boards, a corner board, a downpipe, a door behind its step, a cellar window, the opening of a passage), a shop window for each of the four shops with its wares (yarn, boots, bread, sweets), two carved signs (a kringla, a boot), and a yard's low wall, fence, gatepost, hedge and birch | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/village.py`: shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and their own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. The photos of Bredbyn's main street in `photos/landscape/` (never committed) were looked at for what a wooden house there is made of; no shape is taken from them, no front is a real shop's, and no part has a letter, a numeral or a mark. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
 | `art/baked/aventyr2/olympia.glb` | Olympia's red hall and timber stand, for Äventyr 2: the hall's boards and battens, its windows set into the wall with their sills, its gutter, downpipes and doors. Interpreted from photographs, which are not in it; its name in white in the game's own Playpen Sans at Olov's request (4 November 2026), and no crest or sponsor's board. | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/olympia.py`: shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and their own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. The photos of Bredbyn's main street in `photos/landscape/` (never committed) were looked at for what a wooden house there is made of; no shape is taken from them, and no part has another letter, a numeral or a mark. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
 | `art/blender/a2-nature.py`, `art/blender/kit-tools.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/nature.glb` | Äventyr 2's nature: spruces, birches, a pine, boulders, rock shelves and faces, stumps, branches, logs and bulrushes | Made for this game in Blender, in code, from nothing but its own shapes |
-| `art/blender/a2-creatures.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/creatures.glb` | The two trägubbar, the owl sitting and in flight, and the otter | Made for this game in Blender, in code. The trägubbar are from their description, and have not been held up to Pappa's picture |
-| `art/blender/a2-props.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/props.glb` | Flower pot, rubber boot, umbrella, raft, jetty post, lantern, rain barrel, watering can, pumpkin, the family's silver hatchback (no badge or plate) and a grey estate | Made for this game in Blender, in code |
+| `art/blender/a2-creatures.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/creatures.glb` | The two trägubbar, the owl sitting and in flight, the otter, and Älven's beaver (sitting up with a birch stick in its paws; its head, its flat scaly tail on its hinge and the stick as parts of their own) | Made for this game in Blender, in code. The trägubbar are from their description, and have not been held up to Pappa's picture. The beaver (9 November 2026) is made from nothing but its own shapes and painted corners: no picture, model or texture from anyone else |
+| `art/blender/a2-props.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/props.glb` | Flower pot, rubber boot, umbrella, raft, jetty post, lantern, rain barrel, watering can, pumpkin, the family's silver five-door electric hatchback and the grey estate that drives past in Byn i stormen (9 November 2026: each body one smooth shell with its glass, lamps, trim, door seams and mirrors laid on it, its wheels on pivots of their own at the axles, tyres, spoked rims and plain caps; no badge, emblem, grille mark, plate or letter, and neither copies a maker's design) | Made for this game in Blender, in code: shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and their own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture, and no downloaded model, logo or reference picture. Nothing in it comes from anyone else |
+| `art/blender/a2-street.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/street.glb` | A grown-up walking past behind Byn's street, as tiny Elof sees one: a long belted coat with its hands in its pockets, trousers with a pressed crease, and laced leather boots with heels, soles and welts, skinned on a small skeleton of its own (hips, coat, and each leg's thigh, calf, trousers' hem, foot and ball) that the game walks (`src/render/passerby.ts`) | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/a2-street.py` (9 November 2026): shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, the weights of its skin worked out from its shape, and its own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. Anonymous: no face, no mark, no letter. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
 | `art/blender/a2-built.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/built.glb` | Slide, picnic table, fence, bridge, steps, firewood, the flower bed, a rowing boat | Made for this game in Blender, in code. The firewood's corners say where on its log they are and the bridge's concrete how it stands in the rain; the game draws the rings, cracks, bark, boards, holes and runs from that in code (`src/render/firewood.ts`, `src/render/concrete.ts`), with no texture |
 | `art/blender/a2-yard.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/yard.glb` | Billsta's woodshed with its winter's firewood (drawn as the stack's is, `src/render/firewood.ts`), the rowing boat turned over on its trestles under a tarp (its loose corner a part of its own), the mailbox, the garden furniture under a tarp, the swings at Flärkenbadet, and Olympia's two goals and its kit table | Made for this game in Blender, in code. No name, number or mark on the mailbox or anywhere else |
 | `art/blender/a2-buildings.py`, `art/baked/aventyr2/buildings.glb` | Äventyr 2's buildings that were built in code: Själevad's church far down the lake in Stormens öga (eight white walls of boards and battens with corner pilasters and round-arched windows, the door under a pediment, a tent roof with standing seams, the lantern storey, the bell turret with its gables and the spire), the beaver's lodge of mud and gnawed sticks on Älven's bank, Olympia's store with its striped awning and its floodlight masts, and Billsta's wooden power poles with their street lamps and wires. The windows' glass is the game's own | Made for this game in Blender by `art/blender/a2-buildings.py` (8 November 2026): shapes built from numbers, colours painted on their corners, and each thing's own shade baked in with Blender's Cycles. No texture. The church is interpreted from the description of Själevad's church in `docs/aventyr-2-reference-study.md`, not from a photograph or a measured drawing; its spire ends in a plain gilded ball. No letter, numeral, crest or mark on anything. Nothing in it comes from anyone else. |
